# ASP.NET MVC conventions

- Controllers thin; business logic in `Services/`
- New customer pages: controller + view + optional view model under `ViewModels/`
- Customer pages set `Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_CustomerLayout.cshtml"`
- Admin pages use default `_Layout.cshtml`
- JSON lists for SPAs go through `*ApiController` with `[Route("api/...")]`
- Prefer `IRoomService` over querying `DbContext` from controllers
- Status checks use `RoomStatus.Available` / `Unavailable`
- After structural C# changes, `dotnet build` the project
